<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 7.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Jan 7.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Monday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	   369.84    2.33</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	   225.90    3.14</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	186.75    8.46</p>
<p> 4   Adel Bton Cement    125.36    1.73</p>
<p> 5   Colonial Coml	 122.95    2.25</p>
<p> 6   Herald Rsc	     86.73    0.98</p>
<p> 7   Forrestania Gold     86.02    2.40</p>
<p> 8   Westral Forest	 85.14    2.35</p>
<p> 9   Countrywide-PP	 83.21    1.14</p>
<p>10   Energy Equity	  71.22    0.99</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	    2.07    0.90</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	   3.08    0.87</p>
<p> 3   Computer Power	  3.66    3.75</p>
<p> 4   Premier Inv	     4.23    0.75</p>
<p> 5   Queensland Cotton     5.80    4.40</p>
<p> 6   Parbury Ltd	     6.25    0.74</p>
<p> 7   BTR Plc		   6.99    6.50</p>
<p> 8   OLS Asia Hldgs	  7.23    0.86</p>
<p> 9   Aust Gold Rsc	   7.40    1.35</p>
<p>10   Renison Goldflds	7.87    5.43</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
